{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Jacob hid them.</b> Idolatry and its appurtenances are not among things that may be buried; rather, one must grind them up and scatter them to the wind or cast them into the sea (Avodah Zarah 43a). And it appears to me that the sons of Jacob did not take the idolatry and its appurtenances from Shechem while it was still prohibited and forbidden to them — for a gentile nullifies idolatry against its will (Avodah Zarah 43a), and here it was already permitted to them — but Jacob commanded to remove it for the sanctity of holiness, so that they would be fit to serve HaShem and to offer a sacrifice before Him, just as he commanded them regarding immersion and changing their garments. And burial would have been sufficient for them, and therefore he hid them under the terebinth, in a place where it would neither be cultivated nor sown."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:39:29.989354105Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}